TEST 38430 -- BGP4+ - BFD fall-over
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-24 15:40-15:52 NZST (device clock 03:40-03:52 UTC), tb470
Build:  awplus_main-20260923-20
DUT:    IE520 3-member VCStack "IE520-stk", AS 65001, 2001:db8:1::1/64 on vlan1
Peer:   IE520-sa (standalone IE520, same build), AS 65002, 2001:db8:1::2/64 on vlan1,
        reached over the static LAG sa3.
        Why not the AR4050S (the 2026-09-22 peer): it has no BFD commands at all. The x230 has
        neither BFD nor a BGP licence. (CAMPAIGN-QUEUE issue I-13.)
        (Replaces the 2026-09-22 UNMEASURED. That attempt never ran `service bfd`, and it used
        `show bfd session`, which is not an AW+ command; the command is `show bfd peer`.)

VERDICT: PASS (with a case-text issue, CAMPAIGN-QUEUE I-14).
         The BFD session comes up with no errors. When BFD's packets are lost, BFD fall-over
         terminates the BGP session within ~2 s. With the case's literal ACL, which stops TCP
         only, BFD correctly stays up and BGP ends on its hold timer (+114.5 s).

CONFIG (both ends, mirrored)
  service bfd              (without it: "% BFD protocol daemon is not running")
  interface vlan1 / ipv6 address 2001:db8:1::{1,2}/64
  router bgp 6500{1,2} / neighbor <peer> remote-as <AS>
    address-family ipv6 / neighbor <peer> activate
  then: neighbor <peer> fall-over bfd
  BGP4+ reached Established before BFD was added. Adding fall-over bfd reset the session once
  ("Last Reset ... due to BGP Notification ... Cease/Other Configuration Change"). It
  re-established at once.

STEP 1 -- "Configure BFD fall-over for BGP neighbour" -> "BFD session should up and no errors"
  DUT show bfd peer:
    peer 2001:db8:1::2 local-address 2001:db8:1::1 vrf default interface vlan1
      Active mode, Status: up, Diagnostics: ok, Remote diagnostics: ok, Peer Type: dynamic
      Local/Remote timers: Detect-multiplier 3, Rx 300ms, Tx 300ms
  Peer show bfd peer: the mirror image, Status: up, Diagnostics: ok
  DUT show bgp ipv6 neighbors 2001:db8:1::2:
    BGP state = Established; "Bidirectional Forwarding Detection is enabled"; hold 90 / keepalive 30
  show log | include BFD|bfd|BGP|bgp: no errors. The only non-command line is
    "BGP[2118]: [NETWORK] Server Sock: Successfully opened a listening socket on port 179".
  -> PASS

STEP 2 -- "Configure an access-list on the peer to stop TCP traffic ... kill the BGP session
          without shutting down the port" -> "BFD should detect that the neighbour is
          unreachable and the BGP session should be terminated"
  On the peer: ipv6 access-list NOTCP38430 { deny tcp any any; permit ipv6 any any }
  on sa3 (ipv6 traffic-filter). Applied 15:43:08. The DUT was sampled every ~4.8 s:
      +3.8 s .. +109.7 s  BGP Established,  BFD Status: up   (MsgRc frozen at 11 from +23 s)
      +114.5 s            BGP Connect,      BFD Status: up
  Peer, after:  "Last Reset ... Notification sent (Hold Timer Expired)"; BFD still up
  -> The session WAS terminated, but by the BGP hold timer, not by BFD. BFD stayed up
     throughout. That is correct BFD behaviour: the ACL passes BFD's UDP, so the forwarding
     path BFD monitors never failed.

  Supplementary (2b): the same ACL, with BFD's own traffic also denied ahead of the permit:
    ipv6 access-list NOBFD38430 { deny tcp any any; deny udp any any eq 3784;
                                  deny udp any any eq 3785; permit ipv6 any any }  on sa3
    first DUT sample (~2 s after the rule readback, which itself took ~5 s):
      BGP Connect, Up/Down 00:00:07 -- the session had already dropped
      show bfd peer: Status: init -> down, Diagnostics: control detection time expired
  -> BFD detected the loss (3 x 300 ms) and fall-over terminated BGP within seconds of the
     filter being applied, instead of the 90 s hold time.

NOTES
  - The peer refuses the traffic-filter on the member ports of a static aggregator:
    "% port1.0.9: Cannot attach ACL to an interface that is a member of a static-channel-
    group. Try attaching the ACL to "sa" interface." It is accepted on sa3.
  - In an IE520 hardware ACL, a rule added later without a sequence number goes to the END
    (seq 12, after the permit), so it never matches. Rebuild the list to put a deny first.
  - Neither unit logs a BFD or BGP state change in `show log`, including the hold-timer
    expiry and the BFD down.
  - `no service bfd` returns the console from (config) straight to exec on both units.
  - Teardown: BGP, the addresses, the ACL and `service bfd` removed on both. Both running-
    configs diff IDENTICAL against their pre-test copies.
